"""2N7002 / 2N7002K — commodity logic-level N-channel MOSFETs in SOT-23.

JEDEC-type 60 V small-signal switching FET, multi-sourced by onsemi, Diodes
Incorporated, Vishay and Nexperia in the same SOT-23 (TO-236AB) outline with
the industry-standard pin map (1 = gate, 2 = source, 3 = drain). Intended for
low-side switching of small loads driven straight from 1.8-5 V logic.

`variant` selects the silicon tier. Every in-stock second source of the
selected tier is emitted: the widest-stocked MPN is the primary part and the
rest are BOM alternates that meet or beat the tier bounds below, so those
bounds are what a design may rely on regardless of what gets stuffed.

 Variant  | V_DS | I_D (T_A = 25 °C)  | R_DS(on) max      | V_GS(th)   | Gate ESD clamp
 2N7002K  | 60 V | >= 300 mA          | 4 Ω @ V_GS 4.5 V  | 1.0-2.5 V  | yes, 2 kV HBM
 2N7002   | 60 V | >= 170 mA          | 7.5 Ω @ V_GS 5 V  | 1.0-2.5 V  | no

The tier R_DS(on) bound is taken at the lowest gate voltage every second
source of that tier specifies. Diodes' bins are specified at 5 V rather than
4.5 V (3 Ω for 2N7002K, 7.5 Ω for 2N7002), which sets the 2N7002 tier bound;
the 4 Ω / 4.5 V bound of the 2N7002K tier comes from Vishay.

Per-source data behind those envelopes; the first MPN of each tier is the
primary part and the others are its alternates:

 MPN                | Manufacturer | R_DS(on) max                     | I_D             | V_GS(th) max | V_GS max
 2N7002KT1G         | onsemi       | 1.6 Ω @ 10 V, 2.5 Ω @ 4.5 V      | 320 mA min pad  | 2.3 V        | ±20 V
 2N7002K-7          | Diodes Inc   | 2 Ω @ 10 V, 3 Ω @ 5 V            | 380 mA 1 in² Cu | 2.5 V        | ±20 V
 2N7002K-T1-GE3     | Vishay       | 2 Ω @ 10 V, 4 Ω @ 4.5 V          | 300 mA          | 2.5 V        | ±20 V
 2N7002-7-F         | Diodes Inc   | 5 Ω @ 10 V, 7.5 Ω @ 5 V          | 170 mA min pad  | 2.5 V        | ±20 V
 2N7002,215         | Nexperia     | 5 Ω @ 10 V, 5.3 Ω @ 4.5 V        | 300 mA @ T_sp   | 2.5 V        | ±30 V

Gate drive from 3.3 V logic
- Both tiers are logic-level: V_GS(th) is 2.5 V max and R_DS(on) is specified
  at 4.5 V or 5 V, so a 3.3 V CMOS output fully enhances the channel. No tier
  in this package relies on a 10 V-only R_DS(on) spec.
- No datasheet in the family guarantees R_DS(on) below 4.5 V. Use the typical
  curves for 3.3 V drive and the 4.5 V max as the design bound: onsemi Figure 5
  gives ~1.7 Ω typical at V_GS = 3.3 V, I_D = 200 mA versus 1.33 Ω typical at
  4.5 V, i.e. about 1.3x. Scaling the tier envelope the same way puts the
  2N7002K worst case near 5 Ω at 3.3 V and 25 °C; multiply by ~1.4 at
  T_j = 85 °C (onsemi Figure 6).
- Worked example at 120 mA: 0.3 V and 36 mW for the onsemi 2.5 Ω @ 4.5 V bound,
  0.48 V and 58 mW at the 4 Ω tier envelope, ~0.6 V if the 3.3 V derating above
  is applied. The 2N7002 tier is 0.9 V at its 7.5 Ω bound, which is why
  2N7002K is the default.
- Gate charge is 0.7 nC at 4.5 V (onsemi) and C_iss is 45 pF max, so a 25 kHz
  PWM output sources ~18 µA average and any MCU pin drives it directly. A
  series gate resistor of 47-220 Ω is still worth adding to damp the gate loop
  and slow edges (100 Ω with 45 pF is a ~4.5 ns time constant, negligible next
  to a 40 µs period), plus a 10-100 kΩ gate pulldown so the FET stays off while
  the driving pin is high-impedance during reset or boot. Neither part is
  included here; this package is the primitive only.

Limits and thermals
- Low-side switching only. Source and drain are not interchangeable: the
  intrinsic source-drain body diode conducts whenever V_S > V_D.
- onsemi 2N7002K power dissipation is 300 mW on a minimum land
  (R_thJA 417 °C/W) and 420 mW on a 1 in² pad (R_thJA 300 °C/W). The I_D
  numbers above are steady-state ratings on the manufacturers' reference
  coupons, so copper area sets the real limit well before the 60 V / 5 A pulsed
  ratings do.
- The 2N7002K tier adds gate-source ESD clamp diodes (onsemi simplified
  schematic, Diodes "ESD protected up to 2 kV"), which is why its gate leakage
  is specified in µA at ±20 V rather than nA. Keep |V_GS| inside ±20 V.

Sourcing notes
- Nexperia's 2N7002K is deliberately not listed as a 2N7002K alternate: it is
  the weakest bin of that tier (5.3 Ω max at 4.5 V, V_GS limited to ±15 V by
  its clamp) and shows no distributor stock, so accepting it as a drop-in would
  break the tier envelope above.
- 2N7002W (SC-70) and 2N7002DW (dual, SOT-363) share the die but not the
  footprint; they need their own packages.

Footprint: SOT95P260X110-3N, an IPC-7351 nominal-density SOT-23 land. Pads are
1.05 mm along the lead by 0.6 mm across it, on a 1.9 mm row pitch with a 2.4 mm
pad-centre span; pads 1/2 face pad 3. The embedded STEP model measures
2.9 x 1.3 mm body, 2.6 mm lead span, 1.1 mm height and aligns with the land
without an extra transform. This is the land the package has always shipped,
kept unchanged so existing consumer layouts stay valid.
"""

Variant = enum("2N7002K", "2N7002")

variant = config(
    Variant,
    default=Variant("2N7002K"),
    help="Silicon tier. 2N7002K is the low-R_DS(on), ESD-clamped tier; 2N7002 is the original weaker bin.",
)

GATE = io(Net)
DRAIN = io(Net)
SOURCE = io(Net)

# Index 0 is the primary part (widest distributor stock in the tier, and the
# MPN the tier's symbol describes); the rest are second sources that meet or
# beat the tier envelope in the docstring, so a sourcing system may swap freely.
_PARTS = {
    Variant("2N7002K"): [
        Part(mpn="2N7002KT1G", manufacturer="onsemi"),
        Part(mpn="2N7002K-7", manufacturer="Diodes Incorporated"),
        Part(mpn="2N7002K-T1-GE3", manufacturer="Vishay"),
    ],
    Variant("2N7002"): [
        Part(mpn="2N7002-7-F", manufacturer="Diodes Incorporated"),
        Part(mpn="2N7002,215", manufacturer="Nexperia"),
    ],
}

_parts = _PARTS[variant]

Component(
    name="2N7002",
    symbol=Symbol(library="2N7002.kicad_sym", name=variant.value),
    part=_parts[0],
    properties={"alternatives": _parts[1:]},
    pins={
        "GATE": GATE,
        "DRAIN": DRAIN,
        "SOURCE": SOURCE,
    },
)
